From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:25:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_pci: Walk the vendor capabilities once in
 vp_modern_probe()

vp_modern_probe() looks for four structures - common, ISR, notify and
device configuration - and walks the device's vendor-specific
capabilities from the start for each one, reading every capability's
cfg_type and BAR until the one it wants. QEMU lists a modern device's
capabilities in the reverse of the order it adds them: PCI
configuration access, notify, device, ISR, common. The search for the
common structure, which comes first, reads all five capabilities, and
the four searches read 28 bytes of configuration space between them.

Walk the list once, keep the first usable capability of each of the
four types, and stop once all four are found. A capability's BAR is
read only when its type is still wanted. The result is the same: for
each type, the first capability of that type whose BAR is in use, and
the BARs of those capabilities in modern_bars. On QEMU the walk reads 9
bytes instead of 28, the PCI configuration access capability's type
and the type and BAR of the other four.

Under a hypervisor every configuration read is a trap. On this
machine's QEMU q35 with six virtio-pci devices it is 114 reads fewer
per boot, out of the 258 that vp_modern_probe() and
vp_modern_map_capability() make (counted from the source and QEMU's
capability order; the 258 were measured with the function tracer, and
114 fewer MMIO exits with the patch). At about 6.7 us a nested exit,
that is ~0.8 ms on the boot's path.

It costs nothing at run time. The capabilities are read as before,
fewer times; vp_modern_map_capability() still reads each structure's
BAR again before it maps it.

Measured on the bench fleet (nested KVM, Xeon 6975P-C, one vCPU, the
workspace's shape), alone this patch moved the first SSH login by less
than the noise. With the other four patches that remove exits from
device setup (the IO-APIC table, the state save at add, virtio's
capabilities, queue_select, the MSI message), the cold first login was
9.4 ms faster, 95% interval [5.7, 14.2], over 120 interleaved boots a
side (2026-11-23), and a restored guest's login did not move.

Local patch for this machine. Not upstream.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern_dev.c | 74 ++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern_dev.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern_dev.c
index 413a8c353..03430963b 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern_dev.c
@@ -103,27 +103,36 @@ vp_modern_map_capability(struct virtio_pci_modern_device *mdev, int off,
 }
 
 /**
- * virtio_pci_find_capability - walk capabilities to find device info.
+ * virtio_pci_find_capabilities - walk capabilities once to find device info.
  * @dev: the pci device
- * @cfg_type: the VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_* value we seek
+ * @pos: offsets found, indexed by VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_* value, 0 where none is
  * @ioresource_types: IORESOURCE_MEM and/or IORESOURCE_IO.
- * @bars: the bitmask of BARs
+ * @bars: the bitmask of BARs the capabilities found use
  *
- * Returns offset of the capability, or 0.
+ * Takes, for each structure type from VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_COMMON_CFG to
+ * VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG, the first capability of that type whose BAR
+ * is in use. A BAR is read only for a capability whose type is still
+ * wanted.
  */
-static inline int virtio_pci_find_capability(struct pci_dev *dev, u8 cfg_type,
-					     u32 ioresource_types, int *bars)
+static void virtio_pci_find_capabilities(struct pci_dev *dev,
+					 int pos[VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG + 1],
+					 u32 ioresource_types, int *bars)
 {
-	int pos;
+	int cap, missing = VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG;
 
-	for (pos = pci_find_capability(dev, PCI_CAP_ID_VNDR);
-	     pos > 0;
-	     pos = pci_find_next_capability(dev, pos, PCI_CAP_ID_VNDR)) {
+	for (cap = pci_find_capability(dev, PCI_CAP_ID_VNDR);
+	     cap > 0 && missing;
+	     cap = pci_find_next_capability(dev, cap, PCI_CAP_ID_VNDR)) {
 		u8 type, bar;
-		pci_read_config_byte(dev, pos + offsetof(struct virtio_pci_cap,
+
+		pci_read_config_byte(dev, cap + offsetof(struct virtio_pci_cap,
 							 cfg_type),
 				     &type);
-		pci_read_config_byte(dev, pos + offsetof(struct virtio_pci_cap,
+		if (type < VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_COMMON_CFG ||
+		    type > VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG || pos[type])
+			continue;
+
+		pci_read_config_byte(dev, cap + offsetof(struct virtio_pci_cap,
 							 bar),
 				     &bar);
 
@@ -131,15 +140,13 @@ static inline int virtio_pci_find_capability(struct pci_dev *dev, u8 cfg_type,
 		if (bar >= PCI_STD_NUM_BARS)
 			continue;
 
-		if (type == cfg_type) {
-			if (pci_resource_len(dev, bar) &&
-			    pci_resource_flags(dev, bar) & ioresource_types) {
-				*bars |= (1 << bar);
-				return pos;
-			}
+		if (pci_resource_len(dev, bar) &&
+		    pci_resource_flags(dev, bar) & ioresource_types) {
+			*bars |= (1 << bar);
+			pos[type] = cap;
+			missing--;
 		}
 	}
-	return 0;
 }
 
 /* This is part of the ABI.  Don't screw with it. */
@@ -223,7 +230,9 @@ static inline void check_offsets(void)
 int vp_modern_probe(struct virtio_pci_modern_device *mdev)
 {
 	struct pci_dev *pci_dev = mdev->pci_dev;
+	int pos[VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG + 1] = {};
 	int err, common, isr, notify, device;
+	int bars = 0;
 	u32 notify_length;
 	u32 notify_offset;
 	int devid;
@@ -252,23 +261,25 @@ int vp_modern_probe(struct virtio_pci_modern_device *mdev)
 	}
 	mdev->id.vendor = pci_dev->subsystem_vendor;
 
+	virtio_pci_find_capabilities(pci_dev, pos,
+				     IORESOURCE_IO | IORESOURCE_MEM, &bars);
+	common = pos[VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_COMMON_CFG];
+	isr = pos[VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_ISR_CFG];
+	notify = pos[VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_NOTIFY_CFG];
+	/* Device capability is only mandatory for devices that have
+	 * device-specific configuration.
+	 */
+	device = pos[VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG];
+
 	/* check for a common config: if not, use legacy mode (bar 0). */
-	common = virtio_pci_find_capability(pci_dev, VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_COMMON_CFG,
-					    IORESOURCE_IO | IORESOURCE_MEM,
-					    &mdev->modern_bars);
 	if (!common) {
 		dev_info(&pci_dev->dev,
 			 "virtio_pci: leaving for legacy driver\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
+	mdev->modern_bars |= bars;
 
 	/* If common is there, these should be too... */
-	isr = virtio_pci_find_capability(pci_dev, VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_ISR_CFG,
-					 IORESOURCE_IO | IORESOURCE_MEM,
-					 &mdev->modern_bars);
-	notify = virtio_pci_find_capability(pci_dev, VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_NOTIFY_CFG,
-					    IORESOURCE_IO | IORESOURCE_MEM,
-					    &mdev->modern_bars);
 	if (!isr || !notify) {
 		dev_err(&pci_dev->dev,
 			"virtio_pci: missing capabilities %i/%i/%i\n",
@@ -284,13 +295,6 @@ int vp_modern_probe(struct virtio_pci_modern_device *mdev)
 	if (err)
 		dev_warn(&pci_dev->dev, "Failed to enable 64-bit or 32-bit DMA.  Trying to continue, but this might not work.\n");
 
-	/* Device capability is only mandatory for devices that have
-	 * device-specific configuration.
-	 */
-	device = virtio_pci_find_capability(pci_dev, VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG,
-					    IORESOURCE_IO | IORESOURCE_MEM,
-					    &mdev->modern_bars);
-
 	err = pci_request_selected_regions(pci_dev, mdev->modern_bars,
 					   "virtio-pci-modern");
 	if (err)
-- 
2.53.0

